From: Cast Hub
Subject: [PATCH] wifi-p2p: leave P2P groups alone when the P2P device is unmanaged

NetworkManager creates an NMSupplicantInterface for every GroupStarted. When the
P2P device is not activating it ignores the group and drops that object; dispose
then calls RemoveInterface, so any group started by another program (here
casthub-p2p, which owns Wi-Fi Direct groups) is torn down within milliseconds.
When the administrator has made the P2P device unmanaged, retire the object
without removing the interface. Managed devices keep the stock behaviour.
---
diff --git a/src/core/devices/wifi/nm-device-wifi-p2p.c b/src/core/devices/wifi/nm-device-wifi-p2p.c
--- a/src/core/devices/wifi/nm-device-wifi-p2p.c
+++ b/src/core/devices/wifi/nm-device-wifi-p2p.c
@@ -846,6 +846,21 @@
         _LOGW(LOGD_DEVICE | LOGD_WIFI,
               "P2P: WPA supplicant notified a group start but we are not trying to connect! "
               "Ignoring the event.");
+        /* Cast Hub: when this P2P device is unmanaged (configured by the administrator), the
+         * group belongs to another program. Dropping @group_iface would dispose it, and
+         * dispose asks wpa_supplicant to RemoveInterface, which tears that group down within
+         * milliseconds. Retire our handle without removing the interface instead. Managed
+         * devices keep the stock behaviour. */
+        if (nm_device_get_state(NM_DEVICE(self)) == NM_DEVICE_STATE_UNMANAGED && group_iface
+            && group_iface != iface
+            && nm_supplicant_interface_get_state(group_iface)
+                   != NM_SUPPLICANT_INTERFACE_STATE_DOWN) {
+            _LOGI(LOGD_DEVICE | LOGD_WIFI,
+                  "P2P: device is unmanaged; leaving the group to whoever started it");
+            _nm_supplicant_interface_set_state_down(group_iface,
+                                                    FALSE,
+                                                    "P2P group not started by NetworkManager");
+        }
         return;
     }
 
